WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
One on the pipeline, if I may.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:11.280
I wonder if you could just update us on your thoughts on the confidence and potential for

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.560
abalacimab.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:20.020
And also, I see that it's still showing us a 2027 readout milestone in the slide deck.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:26.520
Clinical trials is now showing a late December 27 primary completion.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.520
So is that still a 2027 out event, or is the potential for slippage into 2027?

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.280
Thanks so much.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.280
Yeah, thanks, Simon.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.280
So we remain excited about abalacimab.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.500
As a reminder, this is a monthly monoclonal antibody that has shown outstanding, I think,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:50.580
overall pharmacokinetic pharmacodynamics on very well-behaved antibody on factor XI.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:56.600
We've seen with competitor data that factor XI appears to deliver on the promise of very

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.100
strong anticoagulation without increased bleeding risk, which is what the genetics would indicate

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:02.600
for us.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.600
And so we have the study ongoing in patients who are ineligible for NOACs.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.760
And that study, we have upsized that study given the event rates that we saw.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.960
So you can also see that at clinicaltrials.gov.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.700
But we're on track for a readout before the end of the year.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.620
That is a readout at 75% of events, just to be clear.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.660
And then the study would continue if it's not successful at that point, or that doesn't

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.660
meet the stopping criteria.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:38.240
At that point, to finish the number of events in 2028.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.540
And then we evaluate now, or are in the process of beginning additional studies in secondary

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.780
stroke prevention, as well as assessing other indications as well.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.780
So excited about that opportunity.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.280
We think it could be a significant asset if the trials ultimately read out positive.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.280
Great.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.280
Thanks so much.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.280
Thank you.

